        "explanation": "`1` and `1.0` are literally the same value — JavaScript has no separate float syntax that produces a distinguishable type. `Number.isInteger()` checks whether the *value* has zero fractional part, which is why `4.0` (already a whole number) passes but `4.5` doesn't."
