      "expectedAnswer": "`arr.unshift(...items)` mutates the array by adding one or more items to the *beginning*, shifting every existing element's index up — returning the new `.length`, mirroring `push()`. Like `.shift()`, it's O(n) because existing elements must be re-indexed.",
